  - title: Oaks for the far corner
    number: 3
    heartsNeeded: 3
    path: 0
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - There's a corner of the park where the old oak came down in a storm. It's been bare for three years.
    - Acorns from a real tree would be perfect. Five. I'll plant them all, and the strongest one gets the corner. It'll be a hundred years before it's finished, but somebody has to start.
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 11400000, guid: db0b4bbca1f1b064182f4bb119d6cb66, type: 2}
      amount: 5
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: Acorns for the park
      questText: Mateo wants five acorns to plant an oak in the bare corner of the park.
      reminder:
      - Any acorns? Five is plenty. The corner's waiting. Corners are very patient.
      thanks:
      - Lovely. Fat and brown. These will do very well.
      - Here. For your trouble. Come back in a hundred years and sit under it.
    choice:
      enabled: 0
      optionA: 
      replyA: []
      flagsA: []
      optionB: 
      replyB: []
      flagsB: []
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 120
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: Blossom week
    number: 4
    heartsNeeded: 4
    path: 0
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 1
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - It's blossom week. The one week a year everybody notices the park.
    - Rosa brought me a cake. Lena drew the trees. Walt said 'not bad', which from Walt is a medal.
    - Fifty-one weeks of nobody noticing, one week of everybody. That's a fair deal, I think.
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
